    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Forty-Two Acres    This is a fictional retelling of the extraordinary true story of Harvey and Elsie Jespersen, the founders of Bethany Homes for Children. Beginning in 1948 to 1991, the Jespersen’s transformed 42 acres of land into a place of refuge.  With unwavering faith, open hearts, and the help of countless others, they provided care to more than 750 children, changing lives through the healing power of prayer, music, and love.    Faith Based Production    Adapted from the book, “Save My Children: The Story of A Father’s Love” by Emily Wierenga    Written and Directed by Miranda Hamer    Available show dates:  &lt;ul&gt;    &lt;li&gt;Friday May 2nd at 7:30&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;Saturday May 3rd at 7:30&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;Sunday May 4th at 2:00&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;Friday May 9th at 7:30&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;Saturday May 10th at 7:30&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;Sunday May 11th at 2:00&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;Friday May 16th at 7:30&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*NEW* May 17th at 2:00pm&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;Sunday May 18th at 2:00&lt;/li&gt;  &lt;/ul&gt;"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Forty-Two Acres"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventAttendanceMode": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode"
      }
    ]
  },
